{"name":"Divine","hex":"#9a7aa0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Divine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of divine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Divine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Divine (performer)","blocks":[{"text":"Harris Glenn Milstead, better known by the stage name Divine, was an American actor, singer and drag queen. Closely associated with independent filmmaker John Waters, Divine was a character actor, usually performing female roles in cinematic and theatrical productions, and adopted a female drag persona for his music career."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Pink_Flamingos_-_Divine.jpg/330px-Pink_Flamingos_-_Divine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divine_(performer)","wikidata":"Q357786"},{"title":"Divine (rapper)","blocks":[{"text":"Vivian Wilson Fernandes, known professionally as Divine, is an Indian rapper and songwriter. He is credited as one of the pioneers of the Indian hip-hop scene and for bringing it to mainstream attention. His lyrics often reflect his experiences growing up in the chawls of Mumbai, focusing on themes such as street life, struggles, and aspirations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Divine_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Divine_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divine_(rapper)","wikidata":"Q30668325"},{"title":"Divinity","blocks":[{"text":"Divinity refers to the quality, presence, or nature of that which is divine—a term that, before the rise of monotheism, evoked a broad and dynamic field of sacred power. In the ancient world, divinity was not limited to a single deity or abstract ideal but was recognized in multiple forms: as a radiant attribute possessed by gods, as a vital force cushioning nature, and even as a quality glimpsed in extraordinary humans, laws, or acts. The Latin divinitas and its Greek counterparts conveyed something both immanent and awe-inspiring: a presence that could be felt in thunder, justice, ecstasy, fate, or beauty."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Isaac_Oliver_Elizabeth_I_and_the_Three_Goddesses.jpg/330px-Isaac_Oliver_Elizabeth_I_and_the_Three_Goddesses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divinity","wikidata":"Q1379405"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Divine_%28Harris_Glenn_Milstead%29_signature.png/330px-Divine_%28Harris_Glenn_Milstead%29_signature.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Divine_%28Harris_Glenn_Milstead%29_signature.png/330px-Divine_%28Harris_Glenn_Milstead%29_signature.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADivine_(Harris_Glenn_Milstead)_signature.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Glenn_Milstead.png/330px-Glenn_Milstead.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Glenn_Milstead.png/330px-Glenn_Milstead.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glenn \"Divine\" Milstead's high school yearbook photo at age 17 in 1963[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlenn_Milstead.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Divine_eating_feces.jpg/330px-Divine_eating_feces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Divine_eating_feces.jpg/330px-Divine_eating_feces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The scene at the end of Pink Flamingos (in which Divine's character Babs Johnson consumes fresh dog feces) became a significant part of American cinema history and dominated discussion of Divine and John Waters's films for decades to come","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADivine_eating_feces.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Issue_-14_Streeetsound_maagzine.jpg/500px-Issue_-14_Streeetsound_maagzine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Issue_-14_Streeetsound_maagzine.jpg/500px-Issue_-14_Streeetsound_maagzine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Divine on the cover of Streetsound (1986)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIssue_-14_Streeetsound_maagzine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Glenn_Milstead_grave.jpg/500px-Glenn_Milstead_grave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Glenn_Milstead_grave.jpg/500px-Glenn_Milstead_grave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glenn Milstead's grave at Prospect Hill Park Cemetery, Towson, Maryland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlenn_Milstead_grave.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Alexandr_Ivanov_015.jpg/500px-Alexandr_Ivanov_015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Alexandr_Ivanov_015.jpg/500px-Alexandr_Ivanov_015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Transfiguration by Alexandr Ivanov, 1824","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A